  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 206 AM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nLittle change is forecast in the overall synoptic pattern through \nFriday night. This results in persistent ridging across the western \nUS and troughing over the northeast US and Canadian Maritimes. \nThis places eastern Iowa, northwest Illinois, and far northeast \nMissouri in northwest flow aloft through the period. This\nresults in a dry forecast over the next 7 days. Tuesday and \nWednesday look to be the warmest of the next 7 days as winds \nturn to the south and become gusty.\n\nThursday into Friday, the flow aloft begins to flatten to zonal\nflow as a a deep trough digs into the western US. This allows \nfor several disturbances to move across the area. Confidence is\nlow in the timing and placement of precipitation during the \nperiod with limited moisture. Model forecast precipitation is \nless than a tenth of an inch.",
